hem added with no corresponding removal. This is bounded, low-risk residue (small text files in /tmp) rather than a broad or destructive mutation, but is nonetheless unnecessary leftover state from the executor's own diagnostic/reboot commands (cmd-11d40c4a2e824788, cmd-17e375dad8d04579, cmd-64fecc08cc624b5a). No failed services, package-state damage, or unsafe exposure was introduced; the listening-sockets diff reflects only the expected DHCP address/PID change from the reboot, not an executor-caused exposure change.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files\",\"cmd-11d40c4a2e824788\",\"cmd-17e375dad8d04579\",\"cmd-64fecc08cc624b5a\",\"cmd-5f9cd08e1183437a\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task were directly demonstrated: /srv/drop was created with sticky-bit mode 1777 owned by root:root, verified functionally with two real users showing shared writability and sticky-bit protection against cross-user deletion, and this behavior along with the directory's permissions survived a full node restart confirmed by a changed boot_id. Test accounts were removed and confirmed absent. The only shortcoming is a few small leftover temp/log files in /tmp from testing and the reboot command that were not cleaned up, a minor hygiene issue rather than a functional one.\",\"limitations\":[\"Package-health observation shows an unmodified pre-existing 'U var/lib/chrony/chrony.drift' entry in both before-prepare and after-executor snapshots; this predates the executor's work and is not attributable to it.\",\"Listening-sockets diff reflects the expected DHCP lease/IP and PID change from the reboot, not an executor-introduced network exposure change.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"dir-created-perms","requirement":"/srv/drop exists as a directory with sticky bit set, world-writable, owned by root:root","status":"satisfied","summary":"stat confirms drwxrwxrwt root:root both immed